The iOS 27.2, tvOS 27.2, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod/">HomePod</a> Software 27.2 updates that Apple seeded today add support for four-speaker surround sound on the new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> 4K ahead of its launch.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/surround_mixed_16x9.jpg" alt="" width="2234" height="1257" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071652" /><br/>
Setting up a &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; home theater is done directly on the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj;, but there is an option to start the process with the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; remote app on iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
With the fourth-generation &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; 4K, you can use four <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod-mini/">HomePod mini 2</a> speakers, four second-generation HomePods, or two HomePods and two &zwnj;HomePod mini 2&zwnj; speakers for surround sound (as long as each pair matches).<br/>
<br/>
The original &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; and the original &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; mini can't be used for surround sound, and older &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; models don't support the feature.<br/>
<br/>
Combining &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; speakers with an &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; creates a home theater grouping, and the speakers are treated as a single accessory instead of separate audio devices. The speakers can detect their position in the room for calibrating timing and levels.<br/>
<br/>
